      "reason": "Disagree. The split is exhaustive, but it infers cell culture for the raw values `in vitro` and `in_vitro`, which do not explicitly identify cells and could denote an acellular solution. It also maps `in_vitro_cells (purified lipofuscin granules)` to `non-biological/computational context`; purified lipofuscin is explicit biological material, so that child label asserts a non-biological setting not supported by the raw value. The species/system policy forbids adding system identity from ambiguity, so this split needs less specific children."
    },
    {
      "decision_id": "primary_photo_species_d1c4cef652d78434",
      "reason": "Disagree. Although the split is exhaustive and most assignments are literal, `animal_in_vivo (passive transfer ex vivo exposure)` is assigned only to `animal in vivo`. The raw value explicitly contains both an animal-in-vivo scope and an ex-vivo exposure component; collapsing it to the in-vivo child erases an explicit system distinction. It should remain mixed or use a combined literal child."
    }
  ],
